Credits are an in-game currency introduced in the [[Version History##CandyLand Update - Release Notes! 12/12/22|December 2022 update]]. Credits allow players to unlock Brawlers from the Brawler Blast.

Credits can be obtained from the Shop, [[Starr Drops]], the [[Daily Streak]], the [[Trophies#Trophy Road|Trophy Road]], [[Brawl Pass]] tiers, [[Brawl Pass|Quests]] and [[Challenges]]. They could also be given as a compensation for unlocking all the Brawlers of a certain rarity. These Brawlers and costs can vary in Rarity, with Rare Brawlers requiring the least amount of Credits and Ultra Brawlers requiring the most. Once all Brawlers are unlocked, all Credits will go towards unlocking Fame tiers.

==Brawler Blast==
The Brawler Blast is a system that allows for unlocking Brawlers in a given Rarity. The Rarities being given Credits are in a set order, though the exact order is unknown as only the current and next two Rarity unlocks are shown on the Brawler selection screen, on the left side.

Once the amount of Credits for the Rarity are acquired, the player is taken to a target range with cardboard cutouts up to 10 Brawlers of that Rarity. If less than 10 Brawlers in that Rarity need to be unlocked, the remaining targets are replaced by generic cutouts of objects such as the robots from PvE events, popcorn, ducks, cacti, or bottles. Tapping the screen will eliminate one random target per tap starting with the generic cutouts, each time granting a chance to be given one to four Gem Fragments. There is a 65.01% chance of a target not giving Gem Fragments, a 29.84% chance of a target giving one Gem Fragment, 3.57% for two, 1.14% for three, and 0.44% for four.

Gem Fragments can increase the Brawler's Power Level and unlock up to one of each of any upgrade. 1 Gem Fragment grants +1 Power Level. 2 Gem Fragments grants +2 Power Levels, a random Gadget, or a random Gear. 3 Gem Fragments grants +3 Power Levels or a random Star Power. 4 Gem Fragments grants +4 Power Levels, a Hypercharge, or a random Buffie. There is also a limit of one Gadget, one Star Power, one Hypercharge, and one Buffie per Brawler Blast game.

Targets can stop being eliminated when one to four Brawlers are remaining; if two or more Brawlers remain, the player has a choice between them. There is a 50% chance of getting a choice. Of that 50%, 57.14% of that will be two choices, 28.57% will be three choices, and 14.29% will be four choices.

[[Gems]] and [[Brawler Key|Brawler Keys]] can also be used to instantly unlock a select Brawler, but it is only recommended to do so if you want one specific Brawler, as you will not gain the extra Power Levels or unlocks from Brawler Blast. Gems can also be used to top off a Rarity being unlocked, with one Gem being equivalent to 5.4 to 5.5 Credits depending on the Rarity.

