==Starr Road==
{{RemovedContent|section}}
The Starr Road was the system that allowed a player to select a Brawler to unlock with Credits, from the initial addition of Credits in December 2022 until it was replaced by Brawler Blast in September 2026. Players had a choice to select between one to four Brawlers of a given Rarity. Once a Brawler was selected, all collected Credits would go towards unlocking the Brawler. Players could choose to switch which of the given choices will be unlocked at any time, even while credits are being collected. After collecting a certain number of Credits, the Brawler would be obtained, giving one last chance for players to switch.

For the week after a Brawler's release and [[New Brawler Event]], players would be able to choose to switch their Credits to unlocking the most recent Brawler. If the player switched back to who they were originally collecting Credits for, or the player did not unlock the new Brawler within their first week on the Starr Road, they moved to the end of their Rarity's choices. From June 2025 to September 2026, Rare and Super Rare Brawlers were unlocked on Worlds 1, 2, and 3 on the Trophy Road instead of the Starr Road; Rare Brawler unlocks gave one specific Brawler while Super Rare Brawler unlocks gave a choice of every Super Rare Brawler yet to be unlocked.

Brawlers in a given Rarity were predetermined. Brawlers who released before the addition of Credits and the Starr Road were ordered semi-arbitrarily in their Rarities, with formerly Chromatic Brawlers being placed at the end of the then-most-recent point in December 2023, and a few cases where multiple Brawlers became available as options simultaneously. Brawlers who released after the Starr Road were ordered in their Rarities based on their release date, following a sequential pattern of Epic, Mythic, Legendary, Ultra Legendary, then back to Epic. The table below is the Starr Road before its removal, with the addition of Rare and Super Rare Brawlers' locations before being moved to the Trophy Road.

