==Chroma Credits==
{{RemovedContent|section}}
[[File:Chroma Credits.png|left|90px|link=]]
Chroma Credits were an in-game currency similar to Credits. They could be used to unlock Chromatic Brawlers of a player's choosing. Unlike Credits, Chroma Credits could not be obtained from Starr Drops. When you got every Brawler, Chroma Credits could be used for achieving Fame if a player unlocked all Chromatic Brawlers, though unlike normal Credits they would not automatically go to Fame. A maximum of 5000 Chroma Credits could be held.

==Chromatic Shop==
{{RemovedContent|section}}
The Chromatic Shop was a system that allowed players to unlock Chromatic Brawlers. The current Chromatic Brawler available from the Brawl Pass costed 2500 Chroma Credits, the previous season's Chromatic Brawler costed 1250 Chroma Credits, and all the rest of the Chromatic Brawlers costed 500 Chroma Credits each.

Every Chromatic Brawler (except Gale, Surge and Colette) required a certain number of Chromatic Brawlers already obtained to be able to be unlocked. Alternatively, [[Gems]] could be used to instantly unlock Chromatic Brawlers depending on its unlock rarity.

