==History==
*On 12/12/22, Credits, Chroma Credits, Starr Road, Chroma Shop, and Fame were added to the game and replaced [[Brawl Boxes]].
*On 26/01/23, fixed an issue with Fame appearing into player's profiles without unlocking all Brawlers.
*On 25/04/23, the cost of the most recent Chromatic Brawler was decreased to 2500 Chroma Credits (from 4500), and the cost of the previous season's Chromatic Brawler was decreased to 1250 Chroma Credits (from 1500). Unlocking Chromatic Brawlers now unlocks the next three as choices rather than the next two, and Surge and Colette no longer require unlocking at least one other Chromatic Brawler.
*On 24/10/23, the Meteoric Fame was added.
*On 12/12/23, Chroma Credits, the Chromatic Shop, and the Chroma Shower Event were removed from the game. Chromatic Brawlers were each assigned a new price and rarity between Epic and Legendary.
*On 27/02/24, battle card backgrounds, [[Pins]] and [[Profile Icons]] can now be unlocked after reaching a certain Fame level. Fixed an issue preventing players from switching Brawlers in the Starr Road.
*On 29/02/24, fixed an issue that prevented players from switching to unlock [[Kit]] on the Starr Road.
*On 25/06/24, the Alien Fame was added.
*On 01/07/24, fixed an issue where the switching Brawlers button in the Starr Road could disappear.
*On 24/06/25, Rare and Super Rare Brawlers were moved to the Trophy Road, and their Credit costs were removed.
*On 16/12/25, the Starr Force Fame was added.
*On 01/09/26, the Brawler Blast replaced the Starr Road; unlock order per Rarity is now random instead of being tied to release date, and often gives varying amounts of Gem Fragments that can upgrade the unlocked Brawler. Rare and Super Rare Brawlers were moved back to Brawler Blast. The Brawler Blast and Fame screens were consolidated into the Brawler selection screen. The order in which Rarities are unlocked was changed, though the exact extent is unknown.

